SPELLCHECK DICTIONARIES

Mnemo.Infrastructure/Dictionaries/Spellcheck/ holds Hunspell dictionary files
(.aff/.dic pairs) for en, de, es, and nb, used by the WeCantSpell.Hunspell package
(see below) through ISpellcheckService. That service backs the Avalonia rich text
editor only; the packaged app relies on the operating system's own web view for
spell checking instead, and its publish step excludes the dictionary folder, so
none of these files are redistributed in a built copy of Mnemo.

They remain in the repository for a planned in-house spellchecker. Before that
ships with its own bundled dictionaries, their licenses need clearing: de.aff
states its own header, "Copyright (C) 1998-2015 Bjoern Jacke <bjoern@j3e.de>",
derived from the igerman98 dictionary, "License: GPLv2, GPLv3", while en, es, and
nb carry no license header of their own and their provenance could not be
established from the files themselves.


